SETTINGS joystick-type radio toggle: clicking a CONTROL-column joystick radio moves the lit indicator
and updates the bottom status line, bit-identically to DOSBox.

The five CONTROL-column joystick-TYPE radios (NO JOYSTICK / STD JOYSTICK / FLIGHTSTICK W/THROTTLE /
THRUSTMASTER FCS / CH FLIGHTSTICK PRO) did not respond to a click: the handler FUN_0000_6b55 had a
DGROUP base-loss (raw host deref -> SIGSEGV), the five radio-widget dirty flags were WORD-typed (the
patch 318/319 store-width class), and the status line reconstruction (patch 134/135) only ever emitted
the "<TYPE> JOYSTICK SELECTED." string -- but with no joystick present the real builder emits
"<TYPE> JOYSTICK NOT RESPONDING!".  Three asm-verified fixes (vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin,
DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, str-seg = word[DGROUP:0x70] = 0x2d74).

HOW THE CLICK WORKS (asm-verified): a click on a joystick radio reaches the widget ACTIVATE handler
6af0 -> 6b27 (`call cs:[bx+0x6b2d]`, bx = handler id, threaded by patch 319) -> for the 5 joystick
radios the table 0x6b2d entries 0..4 all = 0x6b55.  6b55 (`shr bx,1; movzx ax,byte[bx-0x74a1]; call
6c38`) reads the radio TYPE index (bx>>1 = 0..4) and the type value byte[DGROUP:0x8b5f+index] (the
0x8b5f table is identity 0..4), then calls 6c38.  6c38 (`mov ds:0x8b43,ax; mov si,0x165c; call
[0x2ac]=444f; call 700a; mov byte[0x8b91/94/97/9a/9d],3`) stores the selected TYPE into word[0x8b43],
builds the status via the 444f message builder, and marks the 5 radio widgets dirty.  The dirty-walk
209e then re-paints each via the joystick-radio renderer 6cb6 (`shr si,1; cmp si,[0x8b43]; lit if
equal`, patch 132) -> the lit indicator MOVES to the clicked radio.

1. FUN_0000_6b55 (asm 0x6b55): `movzx ax,byte[bx-0x74a1]` = byte[DGROUP:(index+0x8b5f)]; Ghidra dropped
   the DGROUP base -> a raw host deref of the near-offset (SIGSEGV).  Rebase to g_mem+0x1c000.

2. The 5 joystick-radio widget dirty flags 0x8b91/94/97/9a/9d (4b91/94/97/9a/9d) are BYTEs (asm
   `c6 06 .. 03  mov BYTE PTR ds:0xNN,0x3`) but were typed WORD: the WORD `= 3` writes 0x0003, whose
   high byte clobbers the adjacent widget's renderer-index byte -> the dirty-walk re-paints the wrong
   renderer (no indicator move).  Retype to BYTE (same class as patch 318/319).

3. FUN_0000_6c38 status reconstruction (supersedes the 134/135 inline).  The real builder FUN_1000_444f
   (DGROUP:0x2ac = 0xf69:0x444f, asm linear 0x13adf; reloc section si=0x200 @0x33720 uninstalled in our
   port -> the [0x2ac] far call honestly no-ops) assembles, into its own str-seg scratch buffer
   str-seg:0x62f via the strcat helper 0xf69:0x13f5c, the joystick TYPE-NAME + a device-poll SUFFIX and
   returns si=0x62f.  The TYPE-NAME = node[type][+0x35a] in the str-seg node table @str-seg:0x35a
   (stride 10; node0..4 +35a = 0x3a0"NO"/0x3a3"STANDARD"/0x3ac"FLIGHTSTICK"/0x3b8"THRUSTMASTER FCS"/
   0x3c9"FLIGHTSTICK PRO", all static in the image).  The SUFFIX is device-poll-driven (444f -> 13d93
   -> [0x2dc] int-15h game-port poll):
     - type 0 (NO JOYSTICK): no device -> " JOYSTICK SELECTED." (str-seg:0x3f8) => "NO JOYSTICK
       SELECTED." (byte-identical to the prior default settings frame, patch 135).
     - types 1..4: a physical joystick is required and is ABSENT (the shim has no joystick, exactly like
       DOSBox under xvfb) -> the poll fails and 444f takes its carry/build path 0x13b65 ->
       " JOYSTICK NOT RESPONDING!" (str-seg:0x41f) => e.g. "STANDARD JOYSTICK NOT RESPONDING!".
   Rendered through the unchanged 700a->6d65->5591 drawstring path -> byte-identical to the genuine
   DOSBox reference.

444f-DEBT: the WIDGET move + the no-joystick status line are now bit-verified faithfully.  The LITERAL
444f is NOT fully reconstructed (debt still OPEN, now precisely pinned): 444f is a runtime-str-seg
node-method device STATE MACHINE (node[type][+0x35c/0x35e] = str-seg CODE at str-seg:0x4901.. that
polls/calibrates the joystick; 13ebf/13f0e queue-link helpers; 13d93->[0x2dc] game-port poll; the
SELECTED/RESPONDING/BAD-TYPE/CALIBRATE branches; the si=0x200 reloc-section install + SeedServiceVecs
0x2ac/0x2e0/0x2f0 re-decompile).  The joystick-RESPONDING branch is unreachable in a joystick-less
environment (our shim + DOSBox-under-xvfb agree the device never responds), so this net-effect is the
faithful observable behaviour for the covered flow; the responding branch needs a live-joystick shim +
the str-seg node methods.

Result: byte-identical to the DOSBox reference on the new flow settings-joystick (STD JOYSTICK ->
"STANDARD JOYSTICK NOT RESPONDING!") -- AE=0 native + wasm, native<->wasm 0-diff, deterministic.
Reached only by clicking a joystick radio inside SETTINGS -> the prior flows are behaviour-neutral
(6c38 for type 0 is byte-identical to patch 135's default; the dirty-flag retypes + 6b55 rebase are
touched only on a joystick-radio click; settings / settings-* unchanged).

